  "description": "BUCMES crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C8 H20 N1 O2 1+,C100 H200 Mn5 N8 O64 Sm8 1-,8(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Sm1 (Sm) has 9 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 9 O neighbors; Sm3 (Sm) has 9 O neighbors; Sm4 (Sm) has 9 O neighbors; Sm5 (Sm) has 9 O neighbors; Sm6 (Sm) has 9 O neighbors; Sm7 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm8 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn5 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.435-4.213 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.54-118.42°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C124H244Mn5N17O66Sm8. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 12 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
